Changes from the upstream GhostLock-H80GT tree
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ADDED  exploit/src/targets/honor-HEY2-W09_8.0.0.191/target.h
       HONOR Pad 9 (HEY2-W09 / HNHEY2-Q), MagicOS 8.0.0.191, kernel
       5.10.252-android12-9-ga431fb50f9a2. Kernel-symbol offsets and
       structure offsets were measured from the device's symbolized 191
       kernel and checked against its disassembly.

CHANGED exploit/src/slide.c
       Made the MCAST carrier geometry target-configurable and added the
       HEY2 IPv4 ping-socket path. The 191 profile uses the measured
       carrier shift and socket family.

CHANGED exploit/Makefile
       Default profile is the HEY2 191 profile. The KSU helper sources now
       live in ksu/ rather than ksu/tools/.

ADDED  scripts/fetch-bundle.ps1, scripts/build.ps1, scripts/run-ksu.ps1
       Pinned third-party download and verification, NDK build, and an
       authorization-gated ADB workflow.

ADDED  docs/ and assets/manager-working.png
       Verification notes, offset provenance, safety guidance, and a
       cropped Manager proof screenshot.

REMOVED the upstream per-device target profiles and prebuilt binaries.
        This public tree contains only the verified HEY2 191 profile and
        source code. The H80GT LKM, ksud, magiskpolicy, and Manager APK are
        downloaded by the fetch script and are not redistributed here.

The exploit core remains derived from the upstream IonStack PoC. No claim is
made that the upstream project or KernelSU officially supports HEY2-W09.

KernelSU and the ksu/ directory
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The files under ksu/ are GPL-2.0 (see ksu/LICENSE) and derive from
KernelSU's kernel-side policy and loader work:

  https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU

The fetched kernelsu.ko is a third-party H80GT build from the GhostLock-H80GT
v0.3.1 release. It is not built or redistributed by this repository. The
fetched ksud and magiskpolicy binaries are userspace components from KernelSU
and Magisk respectively; they are likewise not redistributed here.

CVE-2026-43499
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A use-after-free in remove_waiter() in kernel/locking/rtmutex.c on the
futex-requeue-PI proxy-lock rollback path. The upstream fix is commit
3bfdc63936dd ("rtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in
remove_waiter()"). This repository is a research port, not an upstream fix.
